  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB of length MMM, define a function f(B)f(B)f(B) as follows:\n\n\nPick a positive integer XXX\nConsider the array CCC of length MMM, where Ci=Bimod  XC_i = B_i\\mod XCi​=Bi​modX\nXXX is called **good** if CCC is a palindrome\nf(B)=f(B) = f(B)= the number of **good** positive integers XXX for the array BBB\nIf there are infinitely many such XXX, then f(B)=−1f(B) = -1f(B)=−1\nGiven integers NNN and MMM. Find the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all arrays AAA of length NNN satisfying 1≤Ai≤M1 \\leq A_i \\leq M1≤Ai​≤M for all iii. As the answer may be large, output the answer modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input.\n\nThe one and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all arrays AAA of length NNN satisfying 1≤Ai≤M1 \\leq A_i \\leq M1≤Ai​≤M for all iii, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2∗1052 \\leq N \\leq 2*10^52≤N≤2∗105",
      "2≤M≤2∗1052 \\leq M \\leq 2*10^52≤M≤2∗105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2∗1052*10^52∗105.",
      "The sum of MMM over all test cases won't exceed 2∗1052*10^52∗105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
