        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1:\n\nA=[1,1]A = [1,1]A=[1,1]: Any value of XXX is valid. Thus, f(A)=−1f(A) = -1f(A)=−1.\nA=[1,2]A = [1,2]A=[1,2]: Only X=1X = 1X=1 is good. Thus, f(A)=1f(A) = 1f(A)=1.\nA=[1,3]A = [1,3]A=[1,3]: Only X=1X = 1X=1 and X=2X = 2X=2 are good. Thus, f(A)=2f(A) = 2f(A)=2.\nA=[2,1]A = [2,1]A=[2,1]: Only X=1X = 1X=1 is good. Thus, f(A)=1f(A) = 1f(A)=1.\nA=[2,2]A = [2,2]A=[2,2]: Any value of XXX is valid. Thus, f(A)=−1f(A) = -1f(A)=−1.\nA=[2,3]A = [2,3]A=[2,3]: Only X=1X = 1X=1 is good. Thus, f(A)=1f(A) = 1f(A)=1.\nA=[3,1]A = [3,1]A=[3,1]: Only X=1X = 1X=1 and X=2X = 2X=2 are good. Thus, f(A)=2f(A) = 2f(A)=2.\nA=[3,2]A = [3,2]A=[3,2]: Only X=1X = 1X=1 is good. Thus, f(A)=1f(A) = 1f(A)=1.\nA=[3,3]A = [3,3]A=[3,3]: Any value of XXX is valid. Thus, f(A)=−1f(A) = -1f(A)=−1.\n\nThus, the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all possible arrays A=−1+1+2+1−1+1+2+1−1=5A = -1+1+2+1-1+1+2+1-1 = 5A=−1+1+2+1−1+1+2+1−1=5."
